------------------------------------------------------------ 3. Localisation
$ grep -n "seed" repo_snapshot/experiments/adaptive_v10/run_adaptive_benchmark.py
54:  def run_one(system_name, r_base_mode, feedback, seed, pool) -> dict:
57:      env = AdaptiveEnvironment(pool, r_base_mode=r_base_mode, feedback=feedback, seed=seed)
73:      metrics["seed"] = seed                     # metadata: the LOGICAL seed
121: parser.add_argument("--seeds", type=int, default=30)
122: parser.add_argument("--seed-start", type=int, default=0)
149:      seed = args.seed_start + i
150:      r = run_one(sysname, rb, fb, seed, pool)

The CLI loop (148-150) derives a distinct logical seed per episode and passes it
into run_one; run_one records it faithfully into the per-run metadata (73). Both
ends of the chain look correct, which is exactly the reported symptom: recorded
per-run metadata is right while execution is not.

The break is at the one hop in between: the environment is constructed with a
hardcoded literal instead of the parameter.

------------------------------------------------------------ 4. The fix
- repo_snapshot/experiments/adaptive_v10/run_adaptive_benchmark.py
  -    env = AdaptiveEnvironment(pool, r_base_mode=r_base_mode, feedback=feedback, seed=0)
  +    env = AdaptiveEnvironment(pool, r_base_mode=r_base_mode, feedback=feedback,
  +                              seed=seed)

Reversing the defect (defect.json declares this exact one-line substitution).
No random value is pinned, no test is touched, no CLI flag changes, no reported
key changes, no metadata field changes. The logical seed now drives environment
construction, so per-seed episodes are genuinely independent and the cross-seed
spread / paired bootstrap CIs are computed over distinct executions instead of N
replays of one.

